Magicbane is a good thing to have., but it isn't required.  I would
get myself to Basic in firearms.

> About your numbered suggestions:
>
> 1. I'm using a ring of levitation, and gauntlets of swimming. I
> haven't done the lawful quest. I guess I should. (Incidentally, I
> didn't clear the giant room. Would that be more than just random
> loot?) I assume the amulet of flying would be lightning-proof--is that
> the idea?

Well, it's more than that.  In slashem a number of high-level
spellcasters can cast the 'pool of water' spell, which creates a pool
of water under your feet.  If you are surrounded at the time, and you
don't have water walking, swimming, flying, teleportation, magical
breathing or levitation, then you die (AoLS can still save you).  This
can occur with NO warning under worst-case conditions, a spellcaster
can  teleport next to you, summon nasties, and create a pool under
your feet before you get a single counter-move.  Since you rely on an
amulet of reflection, you will not have an "AoLS worn, and this would
kill you completely.

You might consider polypiling amulets for an amulet of magical
breathing, and eat them until you get the intrinsic.

> 3. Reflection is the amulet. I skipped the lawful quest because I
> didn't want to have to wield anything to get reflection. I have a
> silver shield, but I think I can't do martial arts with it.

It is often worth having backup sources of reflection as well as
backup MR.

> 4.  I'll have to get up to speed on spellcasting. Would a helm of
> brilliance be worthwhile here?

Could be.  You don't need to wish for a helm of brilliance, though.
It can be created by upgrading a dwarvish helm IIRC, but that requires
potions of gain level.  Make sure you grease it.

Monks are very good spellcasters.  Ignoring that skill is a huge
waste.

> 5.  I have an amulet of level-drain resistance. I don't think I have
> anything else.

You are a doppleganger, so often your best bet is self-polymorph into
something level-drain proof.

> 6.  I have a +4 submachine gun and over 40 +4 bullets. I have lots of
> bullets, though, and can make more good ones.

Save the +4 bullets for high-level foes which are unaffected by
unenchanted weapons.  +0 bullets do enough damage most of the time
anyway.  The submachine gun is lighter than the assault rifle, but it
has a much shorter range, and a lower rate of fire.

> 7.  My HP is about 270. Yes, I cleared the disgruntled adventurers.
> That bunch carries a lot of wands! (Including, this time, a wand of
> wishing.)

I perfected a way of clearing the DA level without letting them use
any potions or wands (assuming a bit of luck on the map layout).  That
results in a MASSIVE stash of potions and scrolls.

